---
import { ArrowUpRight, Check, Package } from "@lucide/astro";
import Section from "./Section.astro";

interface Props {
	id: string;
}
---

<Section id={Astro.props.id} label="about.md" title="Why it exists.">
	<blockquote class="quote">
		<p>
			Before creating superfile, I tried a lot of terminal file managers, but I was often disappointed by their UI design. So, I built superfile with a primary focus on delivering a refined,
			user-friendly interface.
		</p>
		<footer>yorukot, in the <a class="sf-link" href="/overview">overview</a></footer>
	</blockquote>
	<div class="sf-panes panes">
		<div class="sf-pane">
			<span class="sf-pane__title sf-pane__title--icon"><Package aria-hidden="true" />what's in it</span>
			<p class="sf-pane__body">Several file panels, a preview for text, code and images, a process list, a clipboard, search, sorting, themes, hotkeys you can remap, and a few plugins.</p>
		</div>
		<div class="sf-pane">
			<span class="sf-pane__title sf-pane__title--icon"><Check aria-hidden="true" />a good fit if</span>
			<p class="sf-pane__body">You do everyday file work in a terminal and want to see what you are doing while you do it, without reading a manual first.</p>
		</div>
		<div class="sf-pane">
			<span class="sf-pane__title sf-pane__title--icon"><ArrowUpRight aria-hidden="true" />look elsewhere if</span>
			<p class="sf-pane__body">
				You want the most features. superfile is not the most feature-packed file manager out there. <a class="sf-link" href="https://github.com/sxyazi/yazi">Yazi</a> is a good one that is.
			</p>
		</div>
	</div>
</Section>

<style>
	.quote {
		margin: var(--space-6) 0 0;
		max-width: 36em;

		p {
			margin: 0;
			font-size: 22px;
			line-height: 1.55;
			color: var(--ink);
			text-wrap: pretty;

			@media (max-width: 640px) {
				font-size: 19px;
			}
		}
		footer {
			margin-top: var(--space-4);
			font: 400 15px/1.5 var(--font-mono);
			color: var(--ink-muted);
		}
	}
	/* What's in it across the top, then the two "is it for me" panes side by side. */
	.panes {
		grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
		margin-top: var(--space-7);

		> :first-child {
			grid-column: 1 / -1;
		}
		@media (max-width: 640px) {
			grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
		}
	}
</style>
